{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he came.</b> We know that Moses does not come to Pharaoh without Aaron with him, for he is the interpreter. And now Moses and Aaron are mentioned because both of them were sent away, and [Pharaoh] drove them out at the last, which he did not do in all the plagues:" "<b>To afflict.</b> From the nifal binyan, from the root עני."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "Resolved הושבו (\"were returned/sent back\") as referring to Moses and Aaron being dismissed from Pharaoh's presence, consistent with the context at the end of the locust plague narrative."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:06.952323531Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}